.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MV 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mv
.Nd rename an object in one filesystem commit
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar source destination
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Rename source to destination.
If destination is an existing directory, move source into it under its
own final name.
A destination file can be replaced.
Nothing is copied; both names must be writable through this process's
filesystem view.
There is no cross-filesystem copy fallback and no multi-source form.
.Pp
The rename is one filesystem commit, not a sequence of copy and remove.
The command refuses the same filesystem object, session mount points, and
moving a directory into itself.
It does not preserve access to a removed name or expand the process's
binding.
Success prints nothing; failures are diagnosed on standard error.
There is no
.Fl f
or overwrite prompt.
Options precede operands; a later option word is a path.
.Ql --
ends option processing; use it or a
.Ql ./
prefix for a name beginning with a dash.
Unknown leading options return status 2.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 after a successful rename; 1 for a failed or refused move;
2 for wrong operand count or an unknown leading option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mv /home/operator/draft /home/operator/final
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cp 1 ,
.Xr rm 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
